{
  "_about": "Topic / format consistency rules for every narrator line and on-screen title of a quiz (2026-10-23: a K-pop song emoji quiz said 'Guess the anime from these emojis!'). One rule set, read by core/quiz/line_check.py (the renderer swaps a failing line for a safe template before the TTS) and pipeline/quiz-line-check.js (the AI-line validator and the pre-upload guard). A narration line may only use the word categories its format and topic allow; a line naming another edition, a round count that is not the video's, or a reveal without its own round's answer is a mismatch. Content lines (trivia questions, would-you-rather options and reasons, duel questions) are the items themselves and are only checked for counts / placeholders.",
